    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ka</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Ka</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ka</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are the respective ionization constants for the following reactions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></mfenced></math>.</p><p>(a)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#8652;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math></p><p>(b)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>HC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>&#8652;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>HC</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></p><p>(c)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#8652;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math></p><p>The relationship between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/Math